      "writtenOn": "2024-02-26T17:13:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you have an examples of zephyr fatal errors that result in reason, info and exception all being zero? I wonder if it would be better to map to existing PANIC_SW_* reason?",
      "revId": "1cebc9ef4aa8274bf839a4858b4af1d0597e8111",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "76dc2db7_edadedeb",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/panic.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 168,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-27T09:03:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Basically, all fatal errors that occur within Zephyr codebase have all fields zeroed, right?\nI\u0027ve bumped into this while writing [abort](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/5307705) test that runs on hardware. FPMCU uses newlib with the common [abort](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/lib/libc/common/source/stdlib/abort.c#L10) call implementation, which causes kernel panic. It doesn\u0027t set the reason as it is done in [EC](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/libc/syscalls.c;l\u003d34).",
      "parentUuid": "2c349d83_a3e71171",
      "revId": "1cebc9ef4aa8274bf839a4858b4af1d0597e8111",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c7a198b_621ec884",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/panic.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 168,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-28T16:56:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "abort() \u003d\u003e k_panic() \u003d\u003e z_except_reason(K_ERR_KERNEL_PANIC), so there won\u0027t be much additional info in this case unfortunately.",
      "parentUuid": "76dc2db7_edadedeb",
      "revId": "1cebc9ef4aa8274bf839a4858b4af1d0597e8111",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17e2b8e1_4d26ff52",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/panic.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 169,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-26T17:13:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Typically reason holds PANIC_SW_* and info holds arbitrary context specific info (e.g. PC or assert line number). Exception is sometimes used to hold the task/thread id. This isn\u0027t ideal, but there is existing infrastructure that handles this form. So I\u0027d suggest something like: \npanic_set_reason(PANIC_SW_ZEPHYR_FATAL_ERROR, reason, task_get_current())",
      "revId": "1cebc9ef4aa8274bf839a4858b4af1d0597e8111",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c01524db_a86fdb60",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/panic.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 169,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-27T09:03:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Make sense. One note is that it doesn\u0027t have to be software panic, there is a list of [arch specific errors](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/include/zephyr/arch/arm/arch.h#L62). So I would go for `panic_set_reason(PANIC_ZEPHYR_FATAL_ERROR, reason, task_get_current())`. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "17e2b8e1_4d26ff52",
      "revId": "1cebc9ef4aa8274bf839a4858b4af1d0597e8111",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58982bea_586e4fe9",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/panic.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 169,
